# anakata-ui — shared layer rules

This repo is a **Nuxt layer** extended by anakata-rms, anakata-crm and anakata-engine. It owns:
- the design tokens (`app/assets/css/main.css`) — variable names identical to the prototypes: `--forest, --forest-950/900/700/600, --coral, --coral-600/400, --ivory, --iv62, --iv38, --hair, --sand, --olive, --ok, --warn`, plus the engine's easing curves `--ease, --eo, --eio`
- the mapping of those tokens onto Nuxt UI's variables (`--ui-bg*`, `--ui-text*`, `--ui-border*`, `--ui-primary`, `--ui-radius: 0`)
- the Nuxt UI component overrides (`app.config.ts`) — tuned to the **back office** (RMS and CRM share identical CSS). The engine layers its own size overrides on top in its app.
- fonts (Oswald, Archivo, IBM Plex Mono, Manrope) via @nuxt/fonts
- colour mode: **dark is the default**, light is the alternative (the prototypes' `html[data-theme="light"]` becomes Nuxt UI's light mode; their `:root` is dark)
- shared components, prefixed **`Ank`** (`AnkLabel`, `AnkPill`, `AnkPanel`, `AnkKpi`, `AnkMoney`, `AnkThemeToggle`…)
- composables: `useApi()`, `useMoney()`, `useDates()`
- generated API types (`app/types/api.d.ts`, from anakata-api's OpenAPI spec)

## Rules
- Nothing app-specific here. If only one app uses it, it belongs in that app. Exception: a component two apps will share soon.
- Paths in `nuxt.config.ts` use `createResolver(import.meta.url)` so they resolve when extended.
- Every visual value is taken from the prototypes' CSS — never from Nuxt UI defaults or taste. When in doubt, open `prototype/index.html` (RMS), find the class, copy the values.
- Keep `@nuxt/ui` and `tailwindcss` versions identical to the three apps.
- The `.playground` app contains a **style guide page** showing every token, every themed Nuxt UI component and every `Ank*` component in both themes. Update it whenever you add or change something.
- Releases: semantic version git tags (`v0.1.0`, `v0.2.0`…). Breaking changes bump the minor while < 1.0. Write a line in `CHANGELOG.md` per release.
